# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, we will show how to choose subspace dimensions in the `qiskit_addon_sqd` package to post-process quantum samples using the [self-consistent configuration recovery technique](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"
msgstr "Sa gabay na ito, ipapakita namin kung paano pumili ng mga dimensyon ng subspace sa package na `qiskit_addon_sqd` para i-post-process ang mga quantum sample gamit ang [self-consistent configuration recovery technique](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More importantly, this guide also highlights some differences in the behavior in the subspace construction when run in `open_shell = False` or `open_shell = True` modes:\n"
msgstr "Higit sa lahat, binibigyang-diin din ng gabay na ito ang ilang pagkakaiba sa gawi ng pagbuo ng subspace kapag pinatakbo sa mode na `open_shell = False` o `open_shell = True`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = False` only works when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is the same.\n"
msgstr "Gumagana lang ang `open_shell = False` kapag pareho ang bilang ng mga spin-up at spin-down na electron.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = True` must be used when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is different. It can also be used when the number of spin-up and spin-down electrons is the same. However, in this last case, there is a difference in the sizes of the subspaces generated between `open_shell = False` and `open_shell = True`, as discussed in this guide.\n"
msgstr "Dapat gamitin ang `open_shell = True` kapag magkaiba ang bilang ng mga spin-up at spin-down na electron. Magagamit din ito kapag pareho ang bilang ng mga spin-up at spin-down na electron. Gayunpaman, sa huling kasong ito, may pagkakaiba sa laki ng mga subspace na nabubuo sa pagitan ng `open_shell = False` at `open_shell = True`, gaya ng tinalakay sa gabay na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**NOTE:** Some of the electronic-configuration (bitstring) manipulations in this package have as a goal to preserve the total spin symmetry $S^2$. Standard Selected Configuration Interaction (SCI) solvers cannot impose $S^2$ conservation exactly. Consequently, they do so approximately via a Lagrange multiplier.\n"
msgstr "**TANDAAN:** Ang ilan sa mga manipulasyon ng electronic-configuration (bitstring) sa package na ito ay may layuning panatilihin ang kabuuang spin symmetry na $S^2$. Hindi eksaktong maipapatupad ng mga karaniwang Selected Configuration Interaction (SCI) solver ang konserbasyon ng $S^2$. Kaya, tinatantiya lang nila ito sa pamamagitan ng Lagrange multiplier.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of electronic configurations entering the eigenstate solver can also have a strong effect in the conservation of spin. For example, in a (2-electron, 2-orbital) system, one can sample the configuration $|1001\\rangle$ (having a single spin-up excitation over the RHF state $|0101\\rangle$), which is a linear combination of the open-shell singlet and triplet states, respectively $(|1001\\rangle ± |0110\\rangle) /\\sqrt{2}$. If the configuration |0110⟩ is not sampled, one can construct neither eigenfunction of total spin, leading to spin contamination or redundancy (the configuration |1001⟩ is involved in a CI calculation, but has coefficient 0 in the CI vector). Given that a single sample $|1001\\rangle$ is generated in the quantum computer, this is how the `sqd` package handles this situation:\n"
msgstr "Malaki rin ang epekto ng pagpili ng mga electronic configuration na papasok sa eigenstate solver sa konserbasyon ng spin. Halimbawa, sa isang (2-electron, 2-orbital) na sistema, puwedeng mag-sample ng configuration na $|1001\\rangle$ (na may iisang spin-up excitation sa ibabaw ng RHF state na $|0101\\rangle$), na isang linear combination ng open-shell na singlet at triplet state, na ayon sa pagkakabanggit ay $(|1001\\rangle ± |0110\\rangle) /\\sqrt{2}$. Kung hindi nai-sample ang configuration na |0110⟩, hindi makakabuo ng alinman sa mga eigenfunction ng kabuuang spin, na humahantong sa spin contamination o redundancy (ang configuration na |1001⟩ ay kasama sa isang CI calculation, pero may coefficient na 0 sa CI vector). Dahil iisang sample na $|1001\\rangle$ ang nabubuo sa quantum computer, ganito hinahawakan ng package na `sqd` ang sitwasyong ito:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = False`:\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = False`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The $1001$ bitstring is split in half, representing spin-up and spin-down configurations: $10$ (up) and $01$ (down).\n"
msgstr "Hinahati sa gitna ang bitstring na $1001$, na kumakatawan sa mga spin-up at spin-down na configuration: $10$ (up) at $01$ (down).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The list of unique spin-polarized configurations is constructed: $\\mathcal{U} = [01, 10]$.\n"
msgstr "Binubuo ang listahan ng mga natatanging spin-polarized na configuration: $\\mathcal{U} = [01, 10]$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We then consider all possible combinations of $\\mathcal{U}$ elements to form the basis: $\\left \\{ |0101\\rangle, |0110\\rangle , |1001\\rangle , |1010\\rangle \\right \\}$, which contains the singlet and triplet states.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, isinasaalang-alang natin ang lahat ng posibleng kombinasyon ng mga elemento ng $\\mathcal{U}$ para buuin ang basis: $\\left \\{ |0101\\rangle, |0110\\rangle , |1001\\rangle , |1010\\rangle \\right \\}$, na naglalaman ng mga singlet at triplet state.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = True`:\n"
msgstr "`open_shell = True`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contrary to the `open_shell = False` case, we do not combine the halves of the bitstring to form the basis.\n"
msgstr "Taliwas sa kasong `open_shell = False`, hindi natin pinagsasama ang mga kalahati ng bitstring para buuin ang basis.\n"

